WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.850
Despite critics' favorable reception of USA
Network's dark teen drama Dare Me, it wasn't

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:10.019
until the show's ten episodes debuted on Netflix
that it truly garnered attention.

00:00:10.019 --> 00:00:14.480
Now, the cheerleading thriller, based on Megan
Abbott's novel of the same name, is keeping

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:18.260
everyone on the edge of their seats as it
recently hit the number seven spot in the

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:21.380
most-watched TV series on Netflix in the U.S..

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:26.170
Gritty teen dramas are always in season, and
Dare Me captivates audiences in an effective

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:31.749
way by pulling viewers into the lives of cheerleaders
and best friends Beth Cassidy, played by Marlo

00:00:31.749 --> 00:00:35.210
Kelly, and Addy Hanlon, played by Herizen
F. Guardiola.

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:39.030
The story is sent into motion when the new
cheerleading coach Colette French, played

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:43.050
by Willa Fitzgerald, arrives and takes away
Beth's power over the squad.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:47.180
With its promise of blood and its depiction
of the darker side of cheerleading, Dare Me

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.379
more than delivers on the thriller aspect.

00:00:49.379 --> 00:00:53.880
Steve Greene from IndieWire wrote that whenever
a member of the cheerleading squad goes, quote,

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:56.989
"flying through the air, a safe landing is
never guaranteed."

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:57.989
He added,

00:00:57.989 --> 00:01:01.890
"Watching these aerial maneuvers against a
sea of psychological chaos is the contrast

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:06.200
that not only gives this USA series its anxiety,
but [also] its artistry."

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:10.930
Dare Me's success lies in the performances
of its leads and its carefully built atmosphere.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:14.750
USA Network Critics generally agreed that
the series' three leads, who hadn't been in

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:17.220
many notable roles before Dare Me, performed
wonderfully.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:18.220
"I'm the captain.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:20.170
We're not doing captains anymore.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:21.180
No, I'm captain.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.689
This is my squad.

00:01:22.689 --> 00:01:23.799
Wrong.

00:01:23.799 --> 00:01:25.770
It's mine."

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:28.159
The Hollywood Reporter's Daniel Fienberg wrote,

00:01:28.159 --> 00:01:32.590
"Kelly, in particular, has a magnetic pull
to her and an effortless ability to transition

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:34.289
from 'innocent to animalistic.

00:01:34.289 --> 00:01:38.710
[...] Dare Me features a tantalizing blend
of guilty-pleasure trashiness, smart genre

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:42.079
deconstruction and unfiltered, darkly comic
adrenaline."

00:01:42.079 --> 00:01:47.520
Fienberg also compared the show to both Netflix's
You and HBO's Euphoria, but argued Dare Me

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:48.520
was better.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:52.680
Still, if there is one misstep these cheerleaders
make, it's dragging the story on for a few

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:53.930
episodes too long.

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:57.010
Alan Sepinwall of Rolling Stone wrote in his
review of the show,

00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:01.450
"Abbott and her TV collaborators are much
more interested in atmosphere than plot.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:06.270
The latter takes a very long time to materialize,
though the former becomes so intoxicating

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.830
that the long wait begins to feel besides
the point."

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:13.060
In the end, Dare Me isn't here to make anyone
comfortable, but instead to explore something

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.160
dark buried within its teenage leads.

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:19.640
In the wake of the show's meteoric rise to
the top ten most popular series on Netflix,

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:24.030
viewers who've been fans of the series since
it first premiered on USA Network in December

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:26.980
2019 are experiencing a wave of hope.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:30.640
Specifically, fans are hoping that the show's
success on the streaming platform will be

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:35.770
enough for either USA Network itself to reverse
course and renew the series for a second season,

00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:39.380
or for Netflix to pick it up and hand down
a season 2 order.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:40.380
One fan tweeted,

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:43.000
"Can Netflix take Dare Me and make a season
2 [please?]."

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:47.520
Another fan tweeted directly to Netflix, tagging
the company's account and then stating,

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:51.780
"Hey Dare Me is in your top 10 shows and trending,
ya think you wanna pick it up for a season

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:52.780
2 please??"

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:56.510
Even audiences who are just now getting into
Dare Me thanks to its arrival on Netflix are

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:57.890
clamoring for more.

00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:02.220
Fans new and old have joined forces to create
and sign a petition urging Netflix to renew

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:03.950
the show for a second season.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:08.001
This is in addition to the many "save Dare
Me" petitions created at the time the series'

00:03:08.001 --> 00:03:10.810
cancellation was announced in April 2020.

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:15.010
While it remains to be seen whether the requests
will have any significance in the eyes of

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:17.597
Netflix executives, it can't hurt to try.

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:25.207
"You are so close to having everything that
you want."

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:30.310
Fingers crossed — and pom-poms up — that
good news will be around the corner for Dare

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.310
Me.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:34.310
If nothing else, though, at least the series
will be remembered as one that captivated

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:39.790
audiences as soon as it aired its first episode
and continued creating buzz over a year later.

